#uuid "5b49dffc-ef34-51f9-880f-343a17e7f464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{11}}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282461} {:answer/id #uuid "8972d08b-477b-5df8-8798-490e031cacfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{7}}}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282876} {:answer/id #uuid "a2129991-a47b-5a82-ac7c-8e1ca3a89e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{11}}}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283104} {:answer/id #uuid "b46333d5-37ec-5aa4-b7d2-c43db38be685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{9}}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283251} {:answer/id #uuid "c63d1f0f-ee09-585f-b726-ba8a97ddf0c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{9}}}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2129991-a47b-5a82-ac7c-8e1ca3a89e30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{11}}}{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283104} :answer-field/id #uuid "54febd29-2fe4-5926-8377-9b3e1c741602" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "abf52321-10d1-5a8b-a0a2-2f3814ff9431" :question/math-academy-id "q-17045" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\sqrt{{(2-x)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2-x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that $x=2-u.$\n\nComputing our limits of integration, we get\n\n| **$x$** | $0$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **$u$** | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nWe can now solve the integral using our new variable $u,$ remembering to use the new limits of integration:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\sqrt{{(2-x)}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x{(2-x)}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{0}(2-u){u}^{3/2}(-\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{0}(u-2){u}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{0}({u}^{5/2}-2{u}^{3/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{7}{u}^{7/2}-2\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}{u}^{5/2})|}_{2}^{0} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{7}{u}^{7/2}-\\frac{4}{5}{u}^{5/2})|}_{2}^{0} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}({0}^{7/2}-{2}^{7/2})-\\frac{4}{5}({0}^{5/2}-{2}^{5/2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{2}^{9/2}}{7}+\\frac{{2}^{9/2}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{11/2}}{35} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{11}}}{35}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292610 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064210 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2feb2115-bd75-5c09-87cc-f10cf46c182f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Indefinite Integrals of Algebraic Functions Using Substitution"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3244d82b-0c46-53a8-a660-f9290373702b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{7}}-\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt[5]{(1-x)^{4}}+\\sqrt{(1-x)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290834} {:answer/id #uuid "39d5bebf-6cd0-585d-82cb-e1a9d8d22ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt[5]{(1-x)^{7}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt[5]{(1-x)^{4}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt[5]{(1-x)^{2}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290873} {:answer/id #uuid "832e2443-c62a-52bc-a01a-c04f3bfe80ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{7}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291188} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbb02ca-90cb-5702-8097-54a2c304eaff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{2}}{7}-{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291317} {:answer/id #uuid "ef92ec5b-c1fe-5e63-956a-e6526b88cd0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}\\sqrt{{x}^{9}}+\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291634}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "832e2443-c62a-52bc-a01a-c04f3bfe80ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{7}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{3}}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291188} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0bc0d7e-9c01-5db9-a9e1-8f9aad1e4e7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "056e1c78-a9bb-5b9a-a3a2-7b12402a4162" :question/math-academy-id "q-2615" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int {x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=1-x.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-1\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=-\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nWe also note that\n$x=1-u.$\n\nNow we can solve the integral in terms of $u,$ and then express our final answer in terms of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int (1-u)^{2}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int ({u}^{2}-2u+1)\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\int ({u}^{5/2}-2{u}^{3/2}+{u}^{1/2})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-(\\frac{2}{7}{u}^{7/2}-\\frac{4}{5}{u}^{5/2}+\\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{7}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{7}}+\\frac{4}{5}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{5}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{(1-x)^{3}}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
